    "problem": "Find all of the subsets of $A=\\{x,y,z\\}.$",
    "worked_solution": "To find every subset of $A,$ we list out every combination of elements within $A.$\n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/assets/1d7c11586a8fff5f63d46d936fd32c7b5fbfc33a406ddf268bfdd934fe787cdf.png)\n\nNote that we must include the empty set since it is a subset of every set.\n\nBy doing this, we get\n\n$$\n∅,\\{x\\},\\{y\\},\\{z\\},\\{x,y\\},\\{x,z\\},\\{y,z\\},\\{x,y,z\\}.\n$$",
